  "term": "counterfactual",
  "definition": "A counterfactual is a \"what-if\" explanation that shows how a different outcome could be reached if some relevant factors were changed. In this source, counterfactual reasoning is used to generate plausible, practical alternatives that help make a prediction or decision more understandable and actionable.",
